{% block header %}
  <header class="fade-in">
    <h1 class="page-title">The Field</h1>
    <div class="subhead">The room that comes <em>next.</em></div>
  </header>
  <div class="divider fade-in"><span class="colophon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="6" y="0" width="8.49" height="8.49" rx="1" transform="rotate(45 6 0)" fill="none" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="1"/></svg></span></div>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <main id="main-content" class="fade-in retreat-layout">
    <section class="retreat-main">
      <p>If you've been reading Field Notes, you already know the territory.</p>
      <p>The questions that come back no matter how much you achieve. The gap between who you are at work and who you are when nobody's watching. The sense that something is off in a way that doesn't show up on any dashboard.</p>
      <p>This is where we work on that. Six people. Six weeks. Weekly 90-minute calls, live. Starting in September.</p>
      <p>The conversations start in the calls. Most of what matters happens in between them.</p>
      <div class="retreat-detail">
        <h3>Who this is for</h3>
        <p>People who've been reading Field Notes and recognize something in it they haven't been able to name. Leaders who are performing and quietly hollowing out. People who are done explaining it to others and ready to sit with it directly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="retreat-detail">
        <h3>What we work on</h3>
        <p>Who you are when the performance stops. Why you're here. What you're running from.</p>
        <p>No curriculum distributed in advance. The direction follows what's in the room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="retreat-detail">
        <h3>Before we begin</h3>
        <p>Each person gets 60 minutes with me before the cohort starts. No agenda. I work intuitively — reading what's present, what's in the room, who or what shows up. Some people call it psychic. Some call it mediumship. Some just call it a sense of knowing. Whatever it is, we use it to set the table for the six weeks ahead.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">If any of this landed, <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:chris@chrismccann.co">write me</a>. I'll send details and we'll talk briefly first. The room matters more than the number.</p>
    </section>
    <aside class="retreat-sidebar">
      <div class="retreat-box">
        <div class="retreat-box-label">At a Glance</div>
        <p class="retreat-box-headline">Small on purpose.</p>
        <hr class="retreat-box-divider">
        <ul class="retreat-box-list">
          <li>6 people maximum</li>
          <li>6 weeks</li>
          <li>90 minutes weekly</li>
          <li>Live — not recorded</li>
          <li>60-min intuitive prep included</li>
          <li>Starting September 2026</li>
          <li>$1,500</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </main>
  <div class="retreat-testimonials fade-in">
    <blockquote class="t-featured">
      <p>"You felt the anxiety in my chest and moved it. Energetically speaking, I feel grounded and like I know exactly what to do."</p>
      <cite>Retreat attendee</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <div class="t-grid">
      <blockquote class="t-small">
        <p>"I feel more whole in my being. Everything you helped to illuminate — I'm feeling really, really good."</p>
        <cite>Retreat attendee</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="t-small">
        <p>"My favorite thing about Chris is that he cares about you as a human first before a number or before your job. That makes him different from other leaders I've had."</p>
        <cite>Former direct report</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block subscribe %}
  <div id="signup" class="signup-section fade-in">
    <h2>Field Notes</h2>
    <p>Cohort announcements go to the newsletter first.</p>
    <form id="pageSubscribe" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 0; max-width: 380px; width: 100%;">
      <input type="email" id="pageEmail" required placeholder="Your email" aria-label="Email address" style="flex: 1; padding: 10px 14px; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--light-gray); border-right: none; background: #fff; color: var(--black); outline: none; min-width: 0;">
      <button type="submit" id="pageSubBtn" style="padding: 10px 20px; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--black); color: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--black); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; transition: opacity 0.2s;">Subscribe</button>
    </form>
    <div id="pageSubSuccess" style="display: none; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 0.5rem;">You're in. Check your inbox.</div>
    <div id="pageSubError" style="display: none; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: #c0392b; margin-top: 0.5rem;">Something went wrong. Try again.</div>
    <script>
    document.getElementById('pageSubscribe').addEventListener('submit', async function(e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      const email = document.getElementById('pageEmail').value.trim();
      const btn = document.getElementById('pageSubBtn');
      if (!email) return;
      btn.textContent = '...';
      btn.disabled = true;
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/.netlify/functions/subscribe', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ email: email }) });
        if (res.ok) { document.getElementById('pageSubscribe').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('pageSubSuccess').style.display = 'block'; }
        else { document.getElementById('pageSubError').style.display = 'block'; btn.textContent = 'Subscribe'; btn.disabled = false; }
      } catch (err) { document.getElementById('pageSubError').style.display = 'block'; btn.textContent = 'Subscribe'; btn.disabled = false; }
    });
    </script>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
